**Technical Specification Document for Green Valley Farms Irrigation and Crop Management System** **Document Version:** 1.0 **Date:** October 15, 2023 **Prepared by:** Green Valley Farms, Inc. **Location:** 1234 Agricultural Lane, Springfield, IL 62701 **Contact:** info@greenvalleyfarms.com | (555) 123-4567 **1. Introduction** Green Valley Farms, Inc. aims to implement an advanced irrigation and crpo management system to enhance the productivity of our 150-acre soybean (Glycine max) and corn (Zea mays) fields. This system will optimize water usage, increase crop yields by 20%, and ensure compliance with the USDA’s National Organic Program regulations. **2. Requirements** - **Irrigation Infrastructure:** - Installation of 10,000 feet of PVC piping (Schedule 40) for the irrigation network. - Integration of a central pivot irrigation system from AgriTech Solutions, model PVT-2024, covering 80 acres. - Soil moisture sensors (HydroSense Pro) to monitor moisture levels in real-time. - **Crop Management Software:** - Deployment of CropTrak software for monitoring crop health and yiedl projections. - Integration with the USDA’s CropScape for satellite imagery analysis. - Must support data sharing with local agricultural extension offices, such as the University of Illinois Extension. **3. Constraints** - **Budget Limitations:** Total budget not to exceed $250,000, including installation and annual maintenance fees. - **Environmental Regulations:** Compliance wiht the Illinois Environmental Protection Agency’s water usage regulations is mandatory. - **Timeline:** All installations must be completed by March 1, 2024, to coincide with the planting season. **4. Details** - **Livestock Management:** Incorporation of 50 head of Angus cattle (Bos taurus) for sustainable manure fertilization, managed through Livestock Management System (LMS) software from FarmTech Innovations. - **Partnerships:** Collaboration with local suppliers such as Prairie Seeds for high-yield soybean seeds and Heartland Fertilizers for organic compost. - **Training:** Staff training on the new system will be conducted by Green Valley Farms’ agronomist, Dr. Emily Carter, and will include sessions on data interpretation and irrigation scheduling. **5. Deliverables** - Complete installation of irrigation and monitoring